<!--Post: 8131--><!--Time: 1108917950-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8131"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Raedelina<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Raedelina<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 8:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it possible BTK does not see his victims as &#34;victims&#34; and that he regards his &#34;work&#34; as a &#34;gift&#34; to them?  To free them from the earthly binds that govern all of us &#40;gravity, hunger, waste, toil, etc.&#41;?  I think he might watch their suffering as &#34;beauty&#34; or &#34;art&#34; in his own worldview ... it is not a wrong thing.  It is right and good to him.  The most natural and beautiful thing ever, because absolutely everyone must endure death as a consequence of life.  He is helping them secretly, while knowing on the outside that it is morally unthinkable and must be hidden.  It makes the experience much more personal on so many levels.  The most intimate experience ever.  Better than sex, obviously.  He lovingly cherishes these memories.   <BR> <BR>I know this is rather unsavory, but I feel closest to BTK when I think at the same level.  What makes a person notice then stalk another?  What makes a person able to watch another die at his own hand?  And get off on it?  And feel connected to something by this death?  And keep trophies?  And taunt the public?  At different times over 30 years?  Why?  What are the reasons?  Be there and go from that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8131-->
<!--Post: 8134--><!--Time: 1108921567-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8134"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 9:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think he&#39;s just a mean self-serving SOB.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8134-->
<!--Post: 8140--><!--Time: 1108926069-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8140"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Raedelina<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Raedelina<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 11:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A mean self-serving SOB with the most fascinating psyche ever!!!  Kills, taunts, eludes for decades?  A very specific set of circumstances created this personality.  Sick but brilliant.   <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t like opera, but I appreciate its structure and complexity.  So goes with BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8140-->
<!--Post: 8146--><!--Time: 1108930408-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8146"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 12:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK&#39;s pretty disparaging about his victims in his communications and enjoys taunting survivors, so I doubt that he sees himself as helping them in any way.  Who really knows what motivates him at this point, though?  We don&#39;t even know why or how he chooses his victims, or if there&#39;s any significance to it.  We won&#39;t have any light shed on this until: <BR> <BR>&#40;a&#41; LE releases more info on BTK&#39;s letters <BR>&#40;b&#41; BTK is captured <BR>&#40;c&#41; BTK publishes his autobiography <BR> <BR>Alas, &#40;c&#41; is probably the most likely to happen at this point.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8146-->
<!--Post: 8150--><!--Time: 1108931111-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8150"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 12:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One problem there. Without a publisher, he can&#39;t authenticate it. Anyone who publishes it will either be arrested for withholding evidence or being an accomplice in a capital murder. <BR> <BR>Ergo... No catchee, No talkee.... no bookee.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8150-->
<!--Post: 8155--><!--Time: 1108931867-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8155"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 12:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule, this is the electronic age!  BTK can publish his own stuff on the Web -- anonymously! <BR> <BR>There&#39;s one &#34;Blog&#34; host that guarantees anonymity to anyone who wants to publish a blog through them: <BR> <BR><a href="http://invisiblog.com/info/faq/#6" target=_top>http://invisiblog.com/info/faq/#6</a> <BR> <BR>There are probably other places on the Web where this can be done.  I just found that one through a quick Google search. <BR> <BR>BTK can publish his life story to a global audience whenever he wants to.  Anonymity guaranteed. <BR> <BR>Welcome to the 21st century.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8155-->
<!--Post: 8156--><!--Time: 1108932157-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8156"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 20, 2005 - 12:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Re: authenticating:  He could add never-before-seen images as authentication -- if he owns a scanner.  FBI would have to authenticate, and it would be up to them to let the public know whether or not the stuff is authentic.   <BR> <BR>I wonder if LE would tell the public if a BTK self-published work on the Web was authentic?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
